        "original_id": "24b522a5-8fa8-5ce0-b3b3-8213ab39caf3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: \"What Kind of Fool (Do You Think I Am)\"\n- People: Ray Whitley, Rick Hall\n- Organizations: The Tams, FAME Studios, Alabama Music Hall of Fame\n- Places: Muscle Shoals, Alabama\n- Awards: John Herbert Orr Pioneer Award\n\nFacts:\n- In 1964, Ray Whitley wrote \"What Kind of Fool (Do You Think I Am),\" and The Tams recorded it as a single.\n- \"What Kind of Fool (Do You Think I Am)\" was one of many hit records recorded at Rick Hall's FAME Studios in Muscle Shoals, Alabama.\n- In 1985, Rick Hall was inducted into the Alabama Music Hall of Fame.\n- Rick Hall also received the John Herbert Orr Pioneer Award.",
